# Task 21: TD Pathfinding Depth - Evidence Log

## Changes Made

### 1. Zone-based Search (pathfind.rs:110-156)
- Added flood-fill BFS to group contiguous passable cells into zones
- Computes zone connectivity before A* search
- Early exit if start/goal are in different disconnected zones (unreachable)

### 2. MAX_PATH_NODES Raised (pathfind.rs:185)
- Changed from hard `max_nodes` cap to `max_nodes.max(64_000)` as `max_expanded`
- Allows long detours (40+ cells) to complete deterministically instead of stalling mid-search

### 3. Per-terrain Can_Enter_Cell Checks (pathfind.rs:97-116)
- Enhanced `terrain_ok` closure with detailed per-terrain checks beyond coarse `is_passable` flag
- Water terrain blocks ground units (matching original `CellClass::Is_Clear_To_Move`)
- Blocking land types (trees, brick walls, wood walls) explicitly blocked

### 4. Deterministic Tie-breaks Preserved
- State ordering unchanged: `f` score → `g` score → `y` → `x` for consistent ordering
- Edge-following diagonal corner-cutting check preserved (lines 223-229)

### 5. Public API Unchanged
- Function signature `find_path(grid, blocked, start, goal, max_nodes)` preserved
- No call site updates needed

### 6. Edge Case: start == goal returns empty path
- Added early return for start == goal case (line 88-90)

### 7. Test Added: long_detour_succeeds
- Tests 40+ cell detour around long wall line without corner-cutting
- Passes with zone-based search

## Acceptance Criteria Verification

✅ `long_detour_succeeds` test passes (6 pathfinding tests total)
✅ Water blocks infantry (terrain_ok checks is_water_terrain)
✅ No stall on unreachable target → deterministic no-move (early zone check)
✅ fmt/clippy/test all green
✅ Commit ready: feat(td): zone-based pathfinding

